course: dictionary
lesson: 7669
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Properly» is one of them. Look at the words around it and ask: is this about how something is done, how much, or how someone behaves?
explain: «Hold the scissors properly» means in the correct, right way, so you hold them safely and well. «I did not sleep properly» means fully or really: the word not shows that you did not get enough proper sleep.
explain: «Behave properly» means act politely and in the right manner. Each time, try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: «Properly» is an adverb. It tells you how, how much, or in what manner something happens.
fact: «Properly» can mean in the correct or right way, as in «wash your hands properly» for about 20 seconds with soap.
fact: «Properly» can mean fully or really, as in «I did not sleep properly».
fact: «Properly» can mean politely and in the right manner, as in «behave properly».
fact: In informal British English, «properly» can mean very or really, as in «properly cold».
exercise: «Badger wants the bedrooms cleaned properly, with clean sheets and fresh soap.» What does properly mean here? | *In the correct, thorough way | Very quietly | Only now and then | Late at night
exercise: «The silk moth cannot fly properly.» Which meaning fits best? | *Well, in the normal way a moth should fly | Very fast | Only at night | Quietly and slowly
exercise: Ben says, «It is properly cold today.» What does properly mean here? | *Very or really, in informal British speech | Politely | Slowly and carefully | Exactly on time
test: «Zebra stripes help to stop flies landing properly.» What does properly mean here? | Loudly | *In the right, working way, so the flies cannot land | Fully and completely | Politely
test: Mum says, «Please behave properly at the party.» What does she mean? | Be cold | Sleep fully | *Act politely and in the right manner | Be very loud
exam: Which sentence uses properly to mean fully or really? | «Hold the pen properly.» | «Behave properly.» | «Fasten your seatbelt properly.» | *«I did not sleep properly.»
